course: dictionary
lesson: 7542
title: Predatory: hunting and harming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Predatory comes from «predator», an animal that hunts other animals for food. When you see predatory, first look at the words around it: what is hunting, eating, or trying to get something? Those clues tell you the meaning.
explain: «Tiny Partula snails on Pacific islands such as Tahiti were wiped out by a predatory snail that people brought in to eat another pest snail.» The snails that ate other snails are the predators. So predatory means living by hunting and eating other animals.
explain: Predatory can also describe people. In safety lessons you may read about «predatory behaviour», which means an adult trying to trick or harm children, especially online. Context helps here too: the words trick and harm show it is dangerous, so you should never share personal details and should always tell a trusted adult.
fact: Predatory is an adjective; it describes a noun such as birds, animals, or behaviour.
fact: «Predatory» (animals) means living by hunting and eating other animals.
fact: «Predatory» (people) means trying to use or harm others for gain, especially weaker people.
fact: Lions, owls and sharks are examples of predatory animals; they sit near the top of food chains.
fact: If you ever feel unsafe online, never share personal details, and tell a trusted adult straight away.
exercise: «...a predatory snail that people brought in to eat another pest snail.» What does predatory mean here? | *Living by hunting and eating other animals | Slow and shiny | Kept safe in zoos | Found only on islands
exercise: A safety lesson warns about «predatory behaviour» online. What does it mean? | Playing a fast game | Sharing photos with everyone | *Someone trying to trick or harm others, especially weaker people, for gain | Being very polite to new friends
exercise: Which of these is a predatory bird? | Snail | Pebble | Partula | *Owl
test: «Predatory birds» and «predatory animals» are both examples of which part of speech? | *Adjective | Adverb | Verb | Noun
test: Why does the Tahiti story show that predatory animals can cause big changes? | Because zoos bred them in a pond | *Because a predatory snail, brought in by people, wiped out the Partula snails | Because snails are slow and cannot move | Because the snails were wiped out by a predatory snail brought in by people
exam: What does predatory mean in «predatory behaviour» when you are told about adults online? | Living on a Pacific island | *Trying to trick or harm others, especially children, for gain | Hunting animals for food in the wild | Being very kind and helpful
